        "The packet does not explicitly support the wording that interpersonal distance is “the space people keep around their bodies in relation to others.” It only states that interpersonal distance (IPD) and peripersonal space (PPS) reflect related but dissociable representations of space around the body, without defining IPD as maintained distance in social interaction.",
